Before diving into the system architecture, we need to discuss some of the assumptions that we have taken into account to successfully deploy the proposed aggregated
ride-sharing platform.
Assumption 1: To enable secure access to user accounts, all the ride-sharing
service providers (SPs) need to support standardized OAuth-based APIs.
Assumption 2: Since registration is accomplished via smart contract deployed
on the Ethereum blockchain, users must have an Ethereum-compatible Web3 wallet
(e.g. MetaMask) to register on the platform.
